    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG are delighted to present No. 89 Furry Park Road to the market, a deceptively spacious three bedroom semi-detached family home enjoying a superb position in this highly sought-after and mature residential neighbourhood. This attractive bay-fronted property offers generous accommodation extending to approximately 115 sq. m. and presents an excellent opportunity for intending purchasers to create a home tailored to their own requirements.\n\nA particular feature of the property is the impressive 85 ft. long west-facing rear garden, which provides an exceptional outdoor space and significant scope to extend and further enhance the existing accommodation, subject to planning permission (s.p.p.). The property also benefits from generous off-street parking to the front.\n\nThe accommodation briefly comprises a very wide and bright entrance hallway, front living room with attractive bay window, rear lounge, breakfast room, kitchen, shower room and storage room at ground floor level. Upstairs, there are three generously proportioned bedrooms, a family bathroom and separate WC.\n\nSituated just off the Howth Road, Furry Park Road is a quiet and mature residential setting that is particularly popular with young families. The property is ideally positioned within easy reach of Killester DART Station, St. Anne's Park and the Clontarf seafront promenade. There is also an excellent selection of local shops, cafés, restaurants, schools and sporting and leisure facilities nearby, while Dublin city centre is readily accessible by public transport and road.\n\nNo. 89 represents an excellent opportunity to acquire a substantial family home with significant potential to extend and modernise in a prime and convenient location. Early viewing is highly recommended."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 2.28m x 5.67m\nAn impressive wide hallway with storage closet.\n\nLiving Room - 3.61m x 4.20m\nCarpeted, feature tiled fireplace with wooden surround, bay window, coving, pocket doors to the lounge.\n\nLounge - 3.31m x 3.86m\nCarpeted, feature tiled fireplace with wooden surround, coving, door to rear garden.\n\nBreakfast Room - 2.59m x 2.60m\nLinoleum flooring, feature tiled fireplace with wooden surround, storage closet, gas boiler.\n\nKitchen - 1.86m x 2.57m\nLinoleum flooring, fitted kitchen units with tiled splashback, door to rear garden.\n\nInner Hallway - \n\n\nDownstairs Shower Room - 1.49m x 2.18m\nLinoleum flooring, tiled walls, WC, WHB, corner shower.\n\nStorage Room - 1.77m x 2.69m\nDouble garage doors to the front, fully wired.\n\nLanding - 2.31m x 3.27m\nCarpeted.\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.64m x 4.04m\nLinoleum flooring, tiled fireplace, bay window.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.64m x 3.99m\nLinoleum flooring, tiled fireplace.\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.31m x 2.86m\nLinoleum.\n\nBathroom - 1.71m x 2.31m\nLinoleum flooring, semi-tiled walls, bath with overhead shower, WHB.\n\nSeparate WC - \nLinoleum flooring, WC.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Gas fired central heating</li><li> Double glazed windows</li><li> Deceptively spacious accommodation</li><li> 85 ft. long west facing rear garden</li><li> Huge scope to extend (s.p.p.)</li><li> Generous off street parking to the front</li><li> Mature residential neighbourhood close to all amenities</ul>"
      },
